Secretary of State Marco Rubio will travel to Miami, Florida, on June 22 to deliver remarks at the Italy–U.S. Business, Investment, Science and Innovation Forum. The Secretary will meet with Italian Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani to advance U.S.-Italy bilateral cooperation on economic security and critical minerals. Leaders from U.S. and Italian companies and financial institutions will also be in attendance to showcase opportunities for advancing shared investment and economic interests.